  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "overlap_signals",
      "text": "1. COMPARE TWO REGISTERED CHANNELS\nThe same red and green outputs feed metrics, white-overlap views and a binary overlap mask. Named tunnels keep their repeated connections readable.",
      "position": [
        0,
        100
      ],
      "width": 720,
      "attached_node": "split_channels_1"
    },
    {
      "id": "overlap_whole",
      "text": "2. WHOLE-IMAGE THRESHOLDS\nThe unmasked metrics, white overlay and Colocalization Mask share one Costes threshold fit over the complete 3D image. Inspect the scatter and thresholds before interpreting the overlap.",
      "position": [
        1000,
        280
      ],
      "width": 356,
      "attached_node": "colocalization_metrics_1"
    },
    {
      "id": "overlap_roi",
      "text": "3. ROI-RESTRICTED COMPARISON\nBinary Threshold defines an ROI from red-channel values above 30,000. The masked metrics and white overlay fit Costes inside this ROI, so their thresholds can differ from the whole-image branch.",
      "position": [
        1580,
        -140
      ],
      "width": 430,
      "attached_node": "masked_colocalization_metrics_1"
    },
    {
      "id": "overlap_binary",
      "text": "4. EXTRACT THE WHITE REGION\nColocalization Mask is exactly the unmasked white-overlap region: voxels at or above both Costes thresholds. Its Boolean output contains no colour channels, and the ROI is not applied to this branch.",
      "position": [
        1000,
        910
      ],
      "width": 650,
      "attached_node": "colocalization_mask_1"
    },
    {
      "id": "overlap_count",
      "text": "5. CLEAN UP, LABEL AND COUNT\nKeep 3D face-connected regions of at least 20 voxels, label each retained region, then calculate Measure Objects for one row per region. Try a minimum size of 1 and compare row counts. These are connected overlap regions, not original organelle counts or proof of mitophagy.",
      "position": [
        1840,
        910
      ],
      "width": 600,
      "attached_node": "measure_objects_1"
    },
    {
      "id": "overlap_compare",
      "text": "6. DIFFERENT QUESTIONS, DIFFERENT OUTPUTS\nPearson/Manders metrics describe intensity relationships; the white view and Boolean mask show threshold overlap; the final table counts and measures connected overlap regions. For graded RACC colour mapping, open the separate RACC Colocalization example.",
      "position": [
        0,
        750
      ],
      "width": 760,
      "attached_node": "input"
    }
